/* S4 code motion: a sum of two lanes moved once. v.x + v.y commutes with interpolation (can_move_alu_across_interp: fadd of two values interpolated alike) and its product with v.z does not, so the link moves the sum into the vertex shader, into v.x's lane; v.y, every use of which the sum post-dominated, is dead and not stored (try_move_postdominator), so the vertex shader stores x and z only and this shader reads two lanes (pan_shc's record, tools/mali/testdata/pan_shc-out/s4_motion_sum.json). */
precision highp float; varying vec4 v; void main(){ gl_FragColor = vec4((v.x + v.y) * v.z, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0); }
